        "shortHash": "2e848c8",
        "hash": "2e848c8b101b9270caf0dbe4bf3629b8e044f80b",
        "subject": "Make the save retry deliberate instead of accidental",
        "body": "Make the save retry deliberate instead of accidental\n\nThe auto-submit effect listed linkedIds/dismissedIds in its dependencies as\nplain filter().map() results, so they got a new identity on every render and the\neffect re-ran constantly once the deck emptied. That is what made retry-after-\nfailure work — and it would have silently stopped working the moment anyone\nmemoised those arrays, leaving a failed save with no way back and the decisions\nstranded.\n\nBoth arrays are memoised now, the effect runs once, and a failed save surfaces\nan explicit retry in the summary. Same behaviour, but on purpose.\n\nAlso drops three strings the redesign left behind — chip, save and save_plural,\nnone referenced since the header chip became icon-and-count and the save button\ndisappeared — and fixes summaryHint, which still told the user nothing would be\nsaved until they tapped a button that no longer exists.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n",
        "author": {
          "name": "Nived Vengilat",
          "email": "nivedvengilat@gmail.com",
          "time": 1786773022000
        },
        "committer": {
          "name": "Nived Vengilat",
          "email": "nivedvengilat@gmail.com",
          "time": 1786773022000
        },
        "branch": "HEAD"
      },
      "actualWorkers": 1
    },
